1. What HookRelay Is
HookRelay is a webhook infrastructure application. A user creates webhook endpoints, stores the target URL and a generated webhook secret, sends events to those endpoints, records delivery attempts, and can inspect or retry failed deliveries.

The application is also responsible for user identity and access: registration, email verification, login, JWT authentication, current-user lookup, forgot-password OTP, and password reset.

Core mental model
Browser
  ↓
FastAPI route
  ↓
Dependency / authentication
  ↓
SQLAlchemy Session
  ↓
PostgreSQL
  ↓
Webhook / Delivery data

For an outgoing webhook:
Event
  ↓
Find user's webhook
  ↓
Build payload
  ↓
Sign payload with webhook secret
  ↓
HTTP request to target URL
  ↓
Record status / response / error
  ↓
Dashboard displays delivery history

Important distinction
Authentication answers: “Who is this user?”

Authorization answers: “Is this resource owned by this user?”

Webhook signing answers: “Did this event really come from HookRelay?”

Delivery tracking answers: “What happened when HookRelay tried to deliver the event?”

