An events router exists in the architecture and is included by app/main.py. Its exact current implementation should be treated as a separate subsystem from the confirmed webhook CRUD and delivery retry routes.

Event subsystem target:

POST /events/... 
     ↓
Authenticate user
     ↓
Identify webhook
     ↓
Validate ownership
     ↓
Create delivery record
     ↓
Call webhook delivery service
     ↓
Store result
     ↓
Expose delivery history

Exact events endpoint names and payload contract are not fully recoverable from the currently indexed source excerpts, so those details should be verified directly in app/routers/events.py before implementation changes.

15. Webhook Service
The project contains app/services/webhook_service.py and the delivery router calls deliver_webhook().

deliver_webhook(
    target_url=webhook.target_url,
    payload=delivery.event_payload,
    secret=webhook.secret
)

The service is conceptually responsible for constructing the outbound HTTP request, signing it, sending it, and returning the HTTP response or raising an exception. Keep network logic in the service rather than duplicating it across routers.

